  "state": "closed",
  "locked": false,
  "title": "Use `removeprefix` to strip weak ETag indicator in `is_not_modified`",
  "user": {
    "login": "gnosyslambda",
    "id": 266641789,
    "node_id": "U_kgDOD-ShfQ",
    "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/266641789?v=4",
    "gravatar_id": "",
    "url": "https://api.github.com/users/gnosyslambda",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/gnosyslambda",
    "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gnosyslambda/followers",
    "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gnosyslambda/following{/other_user}",
    "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gnosyslambda/gists{/gist_id}",
    "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gnosyslambda/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
    "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gnosyslambda/subscriptions",
    "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gnosyslambda/orgs",
    "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gnosyslambda/repos",
    "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gnosyslambda/events{/privacy}",
    "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/gnosyslambda/received_events",
    "type": "User",
    "user_view_type": "public",
    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "`is_not_modified()` uses `tag.strip(\" W/\")` to remove the weak ETag prefix, but `strip()` works on a character set \u2014 it strips any combination of `' '`, `'W'`, and `'/'` from both ends of the string. This means an ETag value ending in `W` or `/` would get incorrectly trimmed.\n\nReplaced with `tag.strip().removeprefix(\"W/\")` which strips whitespace first, then removes the literal `W/` prefix only. `removeprefix` is available since Python 3.9 and Starlette requires 3.10+.\n\nIn practice this is unlikely to cause issues with the current MD5-based ETags from FileResponse, but the fix makes the code do what it actually intends to do.",
  "created_at": "2026-03-19T06:51:35Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-06-10T11:27:40Z",
  "closed_at": "2026-06-10T11:27:40Z",
  "merged_at": "2026-06-10T11:27:40Z",
